# Context7 + Circles

When working on this mini app, **use Context7 MCP** for Circles-related APIs, patterns, and examples. Do not rely on training data for `@aboutcircles/*` packages or miniapp host behavior.

## When to fetch docs

- `@aboutcircles/miniapp-sdk` — `isMiniappMode`, `onWalletChange`, `sendTransactions`, `signMessage`, host bridge
- `@aboutcircles/sdk-transfers` — `TransferBuilder`, `constructAdvancedTransfer`
- `@aboutcircles/sdk-utils` — `encodeCrcV2TransferData`, `circlesConfig`
- Embedded miniapp flows — wallet lifecycle, tx formatting (`to`, `data`, `value` hex), action pipeline
- CRC transfers, pathfinding, RPC, trust paths, publish/upvote flows

## Context7 library IDs (use directly to skip search)

| Topic | Context7 ID / source |
|--------|----------------------|
| Circles SDK v2 (transfers, RPC, core) | `/aboutcircles/sdk` |
| Official miniapps docs | Query: `embedded mini apps sendTransactions` on docs.aboutcircles.com, or use Context7 `resolve-library-id` for `aboutcircles` |
| Payment / Gnosis patterns | `/aboutcircles/circles-gnosisapp-starter-kit` |

Example prompts for the agent:

```
use context7 with /aboutcircles/sdk for TransferBuilder constructAdvancedTransfer
use context7 for @aboutcircles/miniapp-sdk sendTransactions format
```

## This project's conventions (after fetching docs)

- **Host signing**: trivial txs go straight to `sendTransactions` ([`src/host/testSign.js`](src/host/testSign.js)); CRC txs need `TransferBuilder` + RPC first ([`src/chain/executeTransfer.js`](src/chain/executeTransfer.js)).
- **Tx adapter**: always format via [`formatTxForHost`](src/host/bridge.js) — `value` as hex, `data` as `0x…`.
- **Host RPC**: read `circlesRpcUrl` from host app data ([`src/chain/hostRpc.js`](src/chain/hostRpc.js)); do not assume public RPC works from an iframe.
- **Publish**: 1 CRC unlock then one idea ([`src/data/publishUnlock.js`](src/data/publishUnlock.js)).

## If Context7 is unavailable

Fall back to installed packages in `node_modules/@aboutcircles/` and https://docs.aboutcircles.com/miniapps/embedded-mini-apps — never invent method names.
